# Docker build context exclusions for the Sahm backend (P5.1).
#
# The context is the whole "sahm-ai backend" folder, which also contains a
# virtualenv, a local SQLite database and a .env with real credentials. Without
# this file every one of those bytes is uploaded to the daemon on every build,
# and .env would end up in an intermediate layer.

# --- Virtual environments (hundreds of MB, and never wanted in an image) ----
.venv
venv
env
ENV
.python-version

# --- Python bytecode / build artefacts --------------------------------------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build
dist
*.egg-info
.eggs

# --- Test / lint caches ------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.tox
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov

# --- Secrets and local config ------------------------------------------------
# .env holds DATABASE_URL with a password, TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY and provider
# API keys. It must never enter a build context. `.env.example` is kept.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Local database ----------------------------------------------------------
# Local SQLite artefacts. `sahm.db*` covers sahm.db, sahm.db-journal,
# sahm.db-wal and sahm.db-shm.
sahm.db*
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Runtime artefacts -------------------------------------------------------
var/
uploads/

# --- VCS / editor / CI -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- Ops scratch files -------------------------------------------------------
# Stray debugging helpers that live beside the code during development.
_dump.py
_dump_connectors.py
_netcheck.py
_ipv6.py
_pgcheck.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TESTS DO NOT SHIP IN THE IMAGE -- and here is the consequence.
#
# Consequence: `testpaths = ["tests"]` in pyproject.toml:42 points pytest at a
# directory that does not exist inside the image, so `python -m pytest` in the
# running container fails with
#     ERROR: file or directory not found: tests
# rather than reporting "0 passed". This is deliberate: the image is a runtime
# artefact, tests belong to CI on the host (they need pytest/respx/fastmcp,
# which are `[dev]` extras and deliberately not installed by stage 1).
#
# If you ever want to run the suite inside the image you must (a) delete the
# `tests` line below, (b) install the `[dev]` extra, and (c) accept that you
# have just made a production image larger and more attack-surface-y.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests